# Build output
/bin/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test & profiling artifacts
*.test
*.prof
*.pprof
coverage.out

# Local CGO dev dependencies (SDL2, libwebp, ...) fetched by scripts/
/.deps/

# Editor noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Local release packages (CI artifacts are the shipping builds)
/dist/

# AppImage build scratch (scripts/build-appimage.sh)
/AppDir/
*.AppImage

# Flatpak generated manifest (scripts/build-flatpak.sh substitutes the template)
/packaging/flatpak/_build.yaml
*.flatpak

# Emoji font build scratch (nanoemoji venv + ~4000 upstream SVGs + a 10 MB zip).
# Reproduced from scratch by scripts/build-emoji-font.ps1; never committed.
/_emojibuild/
/_wfsalv/

# Work-in-progress dossiers and reference art for the wave in flight. NEVER
# committed: the folder holds third-party reference material gathered for
# measurement only, so a stray `git add -A` must not be able to publish it.
/docs/wip/

# Local gate/dev helpers written per session at the repo root, and their logs
# (_gate.ps1, _w14gate.sh, _r2checks.ps1, _r2gate.log, ...). The committed entry
# point is scripts/, not these.
#
# Matched by SHAPE, not by name. The patterns here used to spell out the two
# prefixes that existed when they were written (_gate, _w<N>gate), and a later
# review round invented a third: _r2checks.ps1 and _r2gate.log sat untracked and
# stageable because "_r2checks" is neither of them. Every round invents another,
# so the rule is now "a root-level file whose name starts with _ and is a script
# or a log" — which needs no upkeep.
/_*.ps1
/_*.sh
/_*.cmd
/_*.log

# Pre-edit backups left by the wave tooling beside the file they copy.
*.r3bak
